    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Find the value of $k$ and the remaining factors if $(x+1)$ is a factor of $x^3-5x^2+kx+8$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$k=2$; remaining factors: $x-2$ and $x-4$.",
      "worked": "Let $P(x)=x^3-5x^2+kx+8$. Since $x+1$ is a factor, $P(-1)=0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(-1)&=(-1)^3-5(-1)^2-k+8\\\\P(-1)&=2-k.\\end{align*}$$\nThus,\n$$\\begin{align*}2-k&=0\\\\k&=2.\\end{align*}$$\nLong division by $x+1$ and quadratic factorisation give\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=(x+1)(x^2-6x+8)\\\\P(x)&=(x+1)(x-2)(x-4).\\end{align*}$$\nThe remaining factors are $x-2$ and $x-4$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 84
  },
